e free left vertices by alternating paths, an edge not in the matching from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left to right, then the matched edge back; the cover is (left ∖ Z) ∪ (right ∩ Z), in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. It is the one minimum cover with the most left vertices, so it does not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"depend on the matching. O(m √n).","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"bipartition","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bipartition","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15BipartiteGraphs11BipartitionV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumvertexcover(bipartition:)"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumVertexCover()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumVertexCover()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum vertex cover (exact): "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" minus "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":", in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (τ = n − α, Gallai), so the minimum cover avoiding the least vertex of a symmetric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"difference. Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count once. The cost is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":"’s: O(m √n) on bipartite components."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"minimumVertexCover()","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumvertexcover()"}}}